From c325427cf52aab281efb828838252f6c3e4fc9ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "miha.kralj" <miha.kralj@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 03:31:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vpp: add libxdp-dev + libbpf-dev for af_xdp XSK support (M4
 ZC)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The VPP af_xdp plugin requires libxdp (xsk_socket__create, XSKMAP population)
for zero-copy AF_XDP to work. Without these build deps, the CMake check fails
and the plugin falls back to the older non-XSK code path that never creates
XSK sockets — BPF program attaches but XSKMAP stays empty, bpf_redirect_map()
silently fails, and no frames reach VPP.

Root cause found 2026-07-22 on board .185: VPP 25.10 af_xdp plugin built
without libxdp → no xsk_socket__create() → no UMEM/rings → XSKMAP empty →
run_cnt=0 on XDP program.

The dependencies are added to the [dependencies] section (not build_cmd)
because ensure_dependencies() in build.py handles sudo apt-get install
properly, whereas inline sudo in build_cmd may fail in the build container.
---
 scripts/package-build/vpp/package.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/package-build/vpp/package.toml b/scripts/package-build/vpp/package.toml
index 99d72c7..8f1a3d2 100644
--- a/scripts/package-build/vpp/package.toml
+++ b/scripts/package-build/vpp/package.toml
@@ -32,5 +32,5 @@ cp build-root/*.deb ../
 
 [dependencies]
 packages = [
-    "llvm"
+    "llvm", "libxdp-dev", "libbpf-dev"
 ]
-- 
